{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787222697,"nonce":"IbXNUGIihrHbG8YrHG+JKUecd18=","message":"Done, on the design ruled in comments #2–#4.\n\n**What landed.** `sweepPolicy` reads a bounded lookback `L` (`DigestLookback = 2m`) over `alert_cases`\nrather than a bare window, folds it against a per-`(policy, Case)` mark table, and advances a coverage\n*instant* once per tick. `skipped_windows` is deleted tree-wide — the WARN it fed was counting a\nbacklog nothing was ever owed, which is the fiction this ticket named. A week-quiet policy now logs\nnothing and issues no read on the second tick; `digest_tick_test.go` asserts both.\n\nMigration `00070_a_digest_is_a_bounded_lookback.sql`: `notifications.digest_covered_from`/`_to`, and\ntables `notification_digest_coverage` (per-policy cursor) and `notification_digest_cases` (marks).\n\n**Deviation from the letter of the ruling, disclosed.** The ruling named only span columns on the\ndigest row. Two tables were added instead, because a row cannot be the cursor for a policy that sends\nnothing, and this ticket specifically requires coverage to advance without a send. A design review\nruled this DEFENSIBLE — comment #1's \"coverage and 'a digest was sent' have to become two separately\nrecorded facts\" was never displaced, and ADR 0001 fixes the datastore, not the table count.\n\n**The detector.** `ReconcileOrg` (`notify.digest.reconcile`, hourly, `RunOnStart`, `PriorityBackground`)\nreuses `Policy.Matches` in Go, never a SQL anti-join, as ruled. It is forbidden from delivering.\n\n⚠️ **A first cut of the detector reintroduced this ticket's own bug** and was caught in review before\nlanding: its candidate span ended at `now − L` while the tick only examines CLOSED windows, so every\nepisode in the open window was unmarked by construction. On a healthy install with\n`digest_window_s = 86400` that WARNed about ~20 correctly-reported Cases every hour, forever — a false\nalarm on the one number this ticket says must be safe to alert on. Fixed by bounding per policy:\n`Digest.UnreportableBefore` = `max(coveredTo, WindowStart(now) − B·W) − L`. A policy with a zero cursor\nis skipped as \"never examined, owed nothing\" so a brand-new policy cannot announce a day-long gap.\n\n**Residuals, deliberate.** `00070` does no backfill: empty coverage reads as never-examined, so an\nupgrade gets one window per policy on the first tick rather than a flood. Widening a window can still\nleave tail minutes unreported because `notif_digest_uniq` refuses the re-tiled start; those episodes\nstay unmarked and surface in the reconciler. Genuinely abandoned windows past `MaxDigestBackfill` now\nlog once, and only when the cursor actually advanced past them — a stuck policy never logs per-tick,\nwhich is what discredited the old counter.\n\nGates: `just lint`, `lint-reachability`, `helm-check`, `dto-check`, `server-check`, `generate-check`,\n`validators-check`, `ui-build`, `ui-test` and the full `-race` Go suite pass.","files":null}]}